L001152	\begin{abstract}
L001153	  For a
L001154	  class of translation-invariant free-fermion systems
L001155	(including those with uniform nearest neighbor hopping)
L001156	on a $d$-dimensional $L \times \cdots \times L$ hypercubic lattice,
L001157	we prove that, starting from an arbitrary pure initial state,
L001158	the system equilibrates with respect to
L001159	the coarse-grained density within a {\timescale} of order $L$.
L001160	This scaling is optimal,
L001161	since there exist initial states whose equilibration requires time of order $L$.
L001162	Our result establishes $O(L)$ as the equilibration {\timescale},
L001163	as is expected in normal macroscopic systems with a conserved quantity,
L001164	such as total number of particles.
L001165	\end{abstract}
